// F2 prerequisite (2026-09-09): the same T122 gap, on the builtin whose hash
// WRAPS. bebop.bp spells a wrapped 64-bit hash SIGNED in the reserved table and
// UNSIGNED in the dispatch ladder, so the two only agree modulo 2^64 -- compare
// the literals as written and the audit reports 16 shadowable builtins instead
// of 7. sys_wait4 hashes to 10054667876514197585 unsigned = -8392076197195354031
// signed, and it is the signed spelling that had to be added. This construct
// fails closed if anyone ever re-derives that table in the wrong width.
// EXPECT COMPILEFAIL:99 from: function name collides with builtin (F2)
fn sys_wait4(a: i64, b: i64, c: i64, d: i64) -> i64 { 5 }
fn main() -> i64 { sys_wait4(1, 2, 3, 4) }
